<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 463 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 463 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 463 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>It allotted 373 million stg outright in bills and 90 million stg in repos to August 11.</p>
<p>The Bank has now provided liquidity totalling 949 million stg so far on Monday in response to a revised money market shortage forecast of 1.35 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
